#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:68
msgid "External interface application has been built with security-first mindset in place. It contains several mechanisms to make sure that all code in the front end is provided directly by the OTOBO framework."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:71
msgid "In addition, a security standard called `Content Security Policy <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_Security_Policy>`__ headers is now leveraged by the built-in web server. It serves as a last line of defense and in case some unexpected code still makes it to the client, it will make sure that the user’s browser simply refuses to run it."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:74
msgid "However, a use-case still exists in which even a modern web application might still need to run some additional code, provided it is vetted and included by the administrators. One example could be an external integrated chat solution, but could also be an inline code snippet used for external web analytics."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:79
msgid "Including custom scripts can be done in the :doc:`../administration/system-configuration` with the following settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:81
msgid "``ExternalFrontend::ExternalScripts``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:82
msgid "``ExternalFrontend::InlineScripts``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:83
msgid "``WebApp::Server::AdditionalOrigins``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:87
msgid "Web Analytics Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:89
msgid "In this example, we outline the steps to include custom scripts used by a web analytics provider in the external interface application. They will be run each time the application is used in order to track and report the behavior of the user for later analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:92
msgid "We start with the provided code snippet below, from a third party provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:105
msgid "First line of the snippet refers to an *external* resource which should be loaded by the ``script`` tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:107
msgid "In the script block below, we have some *inline* code which is run immediately when the page is loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:111
msgid "Adding External Script Resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:113
msgid "First, we need to include the external script location in the appropriate configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:115
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:131
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:184
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:209
msgid "Go to the *System Configuration* screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:116
msgid "Search for the setting ``ExternalFrontend::ExternalScripts``."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:117
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:133
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:186
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:211
msgid "Click on the setting in order to edit it."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:118
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:134
msgid "In case a value is already present, click on the plus button. Otherwise, proceed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:120
msgid "Enter the full location of the *external* resource in the text field. For example: ``https://www.example.com/track/js?id=UA-XXXXXX-Y``."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:122
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:147
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:193
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:216
msgid "Click on the check mark in order to save the modified setting."
