#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:152
msgid "Rebuilding the External Interface Application"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:154
msgid "In order to apply the changes, we also need to rebuild the external interface application. Drop down to shell, and execute the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:163
msgid "Whitelisting Additional Origins in the Security Headers"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:165
msgid "If you now try to access the external interface application, you will be able to verify that the scripts are included in the code. However, your browser will probably block access to all *inline* and *external* resources, therefore the code might fail with some errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:168
msgid "This behavior is by design, since external resources can only be loaded if they are specifically whitelisted in the *Content Security Policy* headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:170
msgid "To check for blocked code, please use suitable web browser inspection tools. In our example, we will be using Mozilla Firefox and its web console available via *Tools → Web Developer → Web Console* menu item, or via the *F12* shortcut key."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:173
msgid "For the example code snippet, you might receive following errors in the console when the application is accessed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:178
msgid "Browser Console Errors and Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:180
msgid "From the console errors we can see that the external script resource was prevented from being loaded (lines 1 and 3). In addition to that, two evaluation calls were also blocked (lines 2 and 5). All errors reference a *Content Security Policy* rule under the name of ``script-src``, which signals script resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:182
msgid "We need to add both the external resource and the evaluation calls to the additional origins list of the *Content Security Policy* headers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:185
#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:210
msgid "Search for the setting ``WebApp::Server::AdditionalOrigins``."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:187
msgid "In case a value for ``script-src`` is already present, click on the plus button next to it. Otherwise, proceed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:189
msgid "Enter the domain part only of the blocked resource in the text field. For example: ``https://www.example.com``. This allows the external resource to be loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:191
msgid "Click on the plus button next to the field, so another value is added."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:192
msgid "Enter the following directive in the new field, including the quotes: ``'unsafe-eval'``. This allows the evaluation calls to be executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:196
msgid "There is no need to rebuild the external interface application at this point, as the additional origins configuration should be immediately in effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:198
msgid "If you reload the external interface application, you might get some additional errors. In our example, it might be the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:204
msgid "Additional Browser Console Errors and Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:206
msgid "This error points that an additional resource that was also blocked, an image at a specific location (line 1). We can deduce this via the name of the *Content Security Policy* rule ``img-src``, which references an image resource. In order to add it to the whitelist, try the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:212
msgid "In case a value for ``img-src`` is already present, click on the plus button next to it. Otherwise, proceed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:214
msgid "Enter the domain part only of the blocked resource in the text field. For example: ``https://www.example.com``. This allows the external image resource to be loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:219
msgid "Try again to reload the external interface application and check if there are more errors. If not, your scripts are now probably working as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:222
msgid "Unfortunately, it is not possible to predict what kind of resources your scripts might be requiring. But, no worries, you can whitelist most of them, just make sure to follow the trail of hints shown in the browser console log. Find a corresponding header rule in the configuration and update it accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:228
msgid "Some resources might only be requested by others, hence several iterations might be needed until everything is configured properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/administration-area/external-interface/layout.rst:232
msgid "Whitelisting external resources opens potential security risks in your OTOBO application! Only allow those resources that you are sure are not malicious and come from reputable sources. Keep in mind that if something is secure today, does not mean it will be tomorrow. Stay safe!"
msgstr ""

